IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Employment Act 1968 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation
-- "version in force from 5/12/2025" -- THE SHARED VOCABULARY (the keel's core).
--
-- This file is made of DECLAREs only.  It holds the nouns that more than one part
-- of the Act's text will have to name, so that no two parts invent the same noun
-- twice.  There is no rule in it and no #EVAL or #ASSERT.
-- Source text: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from Singapore
-- Statutes Online (inputs/EmA1968.txt).  It is not the official text.  The line
-- numbers in the `-- src:` lines are lines of that file.
--
-- Conventions every module of this encoding follows:
--   * money is a NUMBER of Singapore dollars; a count of days, weeks, months or
--     years is a NUMBER; a calendar day is a `Date day month year`;
--   * an amount or date the Act does not give is a MAYBE, never a made-up zero;
--   * every constructor below is a whole phrase, so that no part's own constructor
--     can collide with one here (a constructor name is global to the merged folder).
--   * a field records a FACT a witness could state.  Whether the fact makes the
--     person an "employee" or a "workman" is a rule: it lives in ea-definitions.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- The parties
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:810 | 10.—(1) Either party to a contract of service may at any time give to
-- src:811 | the other party notice of the firstmentioned party’s intention to
-- src:812 | terminate the contract of service.
@ref s 10(1) (src:810-812)
DECLARE `Party to a contract of service` IS ONE OF
    `Party who is the employee`
    `Party who is the employer`

-- Who an "employer" can be: the kinds s 2(1) names, and the kinds of owner that
-- ss 18, 18A and 113A deal with.
-- src:465 | “employer” means any person who employs another person
-- src:466 | under a contract of service and includes —
@ref s 2(1) "employer" (src:465-466)
DECLARE `Kind of employer` IS ONE OF
    `Employer who is an individual`
    `Employer who is a body corporate`
    `Employer who is a partnership`
    `Employer who is an unincorporated association other than a partnership`
    `Employer who is the Government`
    `Employer who is a statutory authority`
    `Employer who is the personal representatives or trustees of a deceased employer`

-- The people and bodies the Act gives a job to.  Used to say who decides, who may
-- be appointed, who an order is directed to; never as a seat (an official gets none).
-- src:719 | 3.—(1) The Minister may appoint an officer as the Commissioner
-- src:720 | for Labour (called in this Act the Commissioner) and also one or
-- src:721 | more officers as Deputy Commissioner for Labour, Principal
-- src:722 | Assistant Commissioner for Labour or Assistant Commissioner for
@ref s 3(1) (src:719-722)
DECLARE `Official or body the Act names` IS ONE OF
    `Official: the President`
    `Official: the Minister`
    `Official: the Commissioner for Labour`
    `Official: a Deputy Commissioner, Principal Assistant Commissioner or Assistant Commissioner for Labour`
    `Official: an authorised officer`
    `Official: an inspecting officer`
    `Official: an authorised person`
    `Official: a medical officer`
    `Official: the Comptroller of Income Tax`
    `Body: the Employment Claims Tribunal`
    `Body: the Industrial Arbitration Court`
    `Body: the General Division of the High Court`
    `Body: a District Court`
    `Body: a Magistrate's Court`
    `Body: a Youth Court`

-- Who is bringing a claim to the Commissioner (the registration fee differs).
-- src:5538 | (a) where the claim is made by an employee ... $3
-- src:5540 | (b) where the claim is made by an employer ... $20.
@ref Second Schedule (src:5538-5540)
DECLARE `Kind of claimant` IS ONE OF
    `Claimant who is an employee`
    `Claimant who is an employer`
    `Claimant who is a subcontractor for labour`

-- A member of the employee's family or household: the facts that decide whether
-- the person is a "dependant" (s 2(1)), a "child" or "young person" (s 67A), or a
-- "child" for childcare leave (s 87A(8)).
-- src:425 | “dependant” means any of the following members of an
-- src:426 | employee’s family, namely, wife, husband, father, mother,
-- src:427 | child and any adopted or illegitimate child living with or
-- src:428 | dependent on the employee;
@ref s 2(1) "dependant" (src:425-428)
DECLARE `Family relationship to the employee` IS ONE OF
    `Relationship: the employee's wife`
    `Relationship: the employee's husband`
    `Relationship: the employee's father`
    `Relationship: the employee's mother`
    `Relationship: the employee's child`
    `Relationship: the employee's adopted child`
    `Relationship: the employee's illegitimate child`
    `Relationship: the employee's stepchild`
    `Relationship: a child the employee fosters`
    `Relationship: no relationship the Act names`

@ref s 2(1) "dependant" (src:425-428)
DECLARE `Family member of the employee` HAS
    `relationship` IS A `Family relationship to the employee`
    `lives with the employee` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is dependent on the employee` IS A BOOLEAN
    `age in completed years` IS A NUMBER

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Pay
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- The unit a contract of service fixes pay for.
-- src:363 | “basic rate of pay” means the total amount of money (including
-- src:364 | wage adjustments and increments) to which an employee is
-- src:365 | entitled under his or her contract of service either for working
-- src:366 | for a period of time, that is, for one hour, one day, one week,
-- src:367 | one month or for such other period as may be stated or
-- src:368 | implied in his or her contract of service, or for each
-- src:369 | completed piece or task of work but does not include —
@ref s 2(1) "basic rate of pay" (src:363-369)
DECLARE `Basis of pay` IS ONE OF
    `Pay is fixed for each hour`
    `Pay is fixed for each day`
    `Pay is fixed for each week`
    `Pay is fixed for each month`
    `Pay is fixed for some other period`
    `Pay is fixed for each completed piece of work`
    `Pay is fixed for each task`

-- What a contract of service pays for ONE period or ONE piece or task, one line
-- for each item that the Act's three pay terms ("salary", "gross rate of pay",
-- "basic rate of pay") count or leave out.  Every amount is for the same unit,
-- whatever `the amounts are for` says.  The terms count different subsets: for
-- example "gross" leaves out travelling, food and housing allowances but keeps
-- other allowances, "basic" leaves out every allowance, and "salary" leaves out
-- only travelling allowances.  Each term is a function over this record in
-- ea-definitions; none of them is a field.
-- src:605 | “salary” means all remuneration including allowances payable
-- src:606 | to an employee in respect of work done under his or her
-- src:607 | contract of service, but does not include —
@ref s 2(1) "salary" (src:605-607)
DECLARE `Pay for a period` HAS
    `the amounts are for` IS A `Basis of pay`
    `pay for the work, with wage adjustments and increments` IS A NUMBER
    `overtime payments` IS A NUMBER
    `bonus payments or annual wage supplements` IS A NUMBER
    `commissions` IS A NUMBER
    `productivity incentive payments` IS A NUMBER
    `sums paid to reimburse special expenses incurred in the course of employment` IS A NUMBER
    `travelling allowances` IS A NUMBER
    `food allowances` IS A NUMBER
    `housing allowances` IS A NUMBER
    `allowances of any other kind` IS A NUMBER
    `value of house accommodation, electricity, water, medical attendance or other amenity` IS A NUMBER
    `value of a service excluded by order of the Minister` IS A NUMBER
    `value of a travelling concession` IS A NUMBER
    `employer's contributions on its own account to a pension fund or provident fund` IS A NUMBER
    `gratuity payable on discharge or retirement` IS A NUMBER
    `retrenchment benefit payable on retrenchment` IS A NUMBER

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Days and periods
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- The kinds of day the Act tells apart when it says whether a day is paid.
-- src:3701 | (6) Despite subsection (5), an employee is not entitled to paid sick
-- src:3702 | leave on a rest day or on a holiday to which he or she is entitled under
-- src:3703 | section 36 or 88 respectively or on any day of paid annual leave or on
-- src:3704 | a day when he or she is not required to work under his or her contract
-- src:3705 | of service or on a day when he or she is on leave of absence without
-- src:3706 | pay granted by the employer at the employee’s request.
@ref s 89(6) (src:3701-3706)
DECLARE `Kind of day` IS ONE OF
    `Day: a working day`
    `Day: a rest day`
    `Day: a public holiday`
    `Day: a day substituted for a public holiday`
    `Day: a day of paid annual leave`
    `Day: a day of paid sick leave`
    `Day: a day of childcare leave`
    `Day: a day of no-pay leave`
    `Day: a day within a maternity benefit period`
    `Day: a day the employee is not required to work`

-- A stretch of days, first and last day both counted: a salary period (s 20), a
-- benefit period (s 76(1A)), the 14 days before a rest day (Third Schedule).
-- src:1271 | 20.—(1) An employer may fix periods (called for the purpose of
-- src:1272 | this Act salary periods) in respect of which salary earned is payable.
@ref s 20(1) (src:1271-1272)
DECLARE `Period of days` HAS
    `first day` IS A DATE
    `last day` IS A DATE

-- The dates of one employment, from the day it began to the day it ended.
-- src:798 | 9.—(1) A contract of service for a specified piece of work or for a
-- src:799 | specified period of time, unless otherwise terminated in accordance
-- src:800 | with the provisions of this Part, terminates when the work specified in
-- src:801 | the contract is completed or the period of time for which the contract
-- src:802 | was made has expired.
@ref s 9(1) (src:798-802)
DECLARE `Dates of the employment` HAS
    `began on` IS A DATE
    `ended on` IS A MAYBE DATE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Ending the employment
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:3293 | (6) If the employment of an employee who is entitled to childcare
-- src:3294 | leave is terminated (whether by resignation or dismissal, upon the
-- src:3295 | completion of his or her contract of service, or for any other reason)
-- src:3296 | before he or she has taken the entitlement of childcare leave of 2 days
-- src:3297 | for a relevant period, the employee —
@ref s 87A(6) (src:3293-3297)
DECLARE `How the employment ended` IS ONE OF
    `Ending: it has not ended`
    `Ending: the specified work was completed or the specified period expired`
    `Ending: the employee resigned`
    `Ending: the employer dismissed the employee`
    `Ending: it ended in some other way`

-- The ground on which the employer dismissed.
-- src:895 | 14.—(1) An employer may after due inquiry dismiss without notice
-- src:896 | an employee employed by the employer on the grounds of
-- src:897 | misconduct inconsistent with the fulfilment of the express or
-- src:898 | implied conditions of the employee’s service, except that instead of
@ref s 14(1) (src:895-898)
DECLARE `Ground of dismissal` IS ONE OF
    `Ground: misconduct inconsistent with the fulfilment of the conditions of service`
    `Ground: redundancy or reorganisation of the employer's profession, business, trade or work`
    `Ground: some other ground or none`

-- A notice of termination, as the employer or the employee gave it.
-- src:840 | (5) The notice must be written and may be given at any time, and
-- src:841 | the day on which the notice is given is included in the period of the
-- src:842 | notice.
@ref s 10(5) (src:840-842)
DECLARE `Notice of termination` HAS
    `given by` IS A `Party to a contract of service`
    `given on` IS A DATE
    `last day of the notice` IS A DATE
    `in writing` IS A BOOLEAN

-- What a claimant may ask for.
-- src:908 | (2) Despite subsection (1), but subject to section 3 of the
-- src:909 | Employment Claims Act 2016, where a relevant employee
-- src:910 | considers that he or she has been dismissed without just cause or
-- src:911 | excuse by his or her employer, the employee may lodge a claim,
-- src:912 | under section 13 of that Act, for either of the following remedies:
-- src:914 | (a) reinstatement in the employee’s former employment;
-- src:916 | (b) compensation.
@ref s 14(2) (src:908-916)
DECLARE `Relief a claimant may seek` IS ONE OF
    `Relief: reinstatement in the former employment`
    `Relief: compensation`
    `Relief: payment of a sum the Commissioner considers just`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Offences
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- What a court may impose on conviction.  `least fine in dollars` is 0 where the
-- text sets no minimum; a NOTHING means the text states no maximum.  Whether a
-- fine and imprisonment may be imposed together, and any rule for a repeat
-- offender, stay with the section that states them.
-- src:1719 | for contravening section 21, 22 or 23 shall be liable on conviction —
-- src:1721 | (a) to a fine of not less than $3,000 and not more than $15,000
-- src:1722 | or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months or to
-- src:1723 | both; and
-- src:1725 | (b) if the employer is a repeat offender, to a fine of not less
-- src:1726 | than $6,000 and not more than $30,000 or to imprisonment
-- src:1727 | for a term not exceeding 12 months or to both.
@ref s 34(2) (src:1719-1727)
DECLARE `Penalty on conviction` HAS
    `least fine in dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `greatest fine in dollars` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `longest imprisonment in months` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
